{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-84888","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117675","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-84889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117676","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-117677","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-117678","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-117679","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-117680","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-117681","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-84890","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117682","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-84891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117683","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-117684","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-117685","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-84892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117686","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-117687","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-84893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117688","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-117689","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-117690","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-84894","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-84895","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117691","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-84896","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-84897","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117692","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-84898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117693","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-84899","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117694","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-84900","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117695","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-117696","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-117697","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-84901","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117698","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-84903","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117699","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-84905","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117700","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-84907","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117701","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-84909","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84911","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117702","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-84912","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117703","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-117704","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-117705","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-84913","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117706","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-117707","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-84915","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117708","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-84917","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117709","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-84919","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117710","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-84921","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117711","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-84923","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84925","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117712","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-84926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117713","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-117714","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-117715","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-84927","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-84928","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117716","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-84929","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117717","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-84930","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117718","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-117719","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117720","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-117721","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84931","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84933","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84935","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117722","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-117723","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-117724","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117725","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-117726","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117727","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-117728","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84934","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84937","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117729","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-84936","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84939","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117730","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-117731","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-117732","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-84938","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84941","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117733","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-117734","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-117735","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-84940","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84943","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117736","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-117737","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-117738","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-117739","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-84942","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84944","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117740","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-117741","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117742","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-117743","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84945","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-84947","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117744","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-84948","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84951","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117745","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-84950","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84953","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117746","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-84952","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84954","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84956","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117747","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-117748","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117749","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-117750","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84955","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-84957","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117751","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-117752","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-84958","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117753","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-117754","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-84960","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84962","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84964","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117755","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-117756","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]}],"id":"blk-84963","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-84965","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117757","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-84966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117758","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-84967","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117759","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-117760","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117761","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-117762","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84968","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84970","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117763","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-117764","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-117765","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-117766","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-84971","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117767","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-117768","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-117769","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-84973","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117770","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-117771","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-117772","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-117773","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-84975","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84978","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117774","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-117775","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-117776","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-117777","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-84977","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117778","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-117779","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-84979","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117780","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-117781","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-84981","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117782","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-117783","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-84983","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117784","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-117785","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-84985","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117786","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-117787","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-84987","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117788","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-117789","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-84989","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84992","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117790","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-117791","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-117792","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-84991","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84994","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117793","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-117794","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-117795","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-84993","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117796","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-117797","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-117798","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-84995","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84997","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84999","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117799","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]}],"id":"blk-84998","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-85000","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117800","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-117801","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-85001","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85004","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117802","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-117803","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-85003","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85006","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117804","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-117805","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-85005","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117806","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-85007","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85009","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85011","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117807","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-117808","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agente